"""Approximate a sparse negative spelling and word-family feature.

Short ise/iso fragments have the strongest response. Related rise/wise/noise,
size, disease, exercise and desire forms get smaller responses, with a few
translated forms and code-related words included. Ordinary spaced 'is' and
unrecognized tokens get zero: this is not a general contains-'is' test.

The previous token adjusts selected is/iz fragments: endings -al,
-ar, -im, -gn and -ec weaken them; 'factor' strengthens them. The rules
capture prominent training triggers, not all vocabulary-specific variation.
